Three vectors are mutually perpendicular, so the scalar or dot product of two vectors will zero. So,
$\mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{B}=0, \mathbf{B} \mathbf{C}=0,$
So, $\mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{B}=(a \hat{\mathbf{i}}+\hat{\mathbf{j}}+\hat{\mathbf{k}}) \cdot(\hat{\mathbf{i}}+b \hat{\mathbf{j}}+\hat{\mathbf{k}})=0\Rightarrow a+b+1=0\mathbf{B} \cdot \mathbf{C}=\hat{\mathbf{i}}+\hat{\mathbf{j}}+\hat{\mathbf{k}} \cdot \hat{\mathbf{i}}+\hat{\mathbf{j}}+\hat{\mathbf{k}}=\Rightarrow 1+b+c=0\mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{C}=(a \hat{\mathbf{i}}+\hat{\mathbf{j}}+\hat{\mathbf{k}}) \cdot(\hat{\mathbf{i}}+\hat{\mathbf{j}}+c \hat{\mathbf{k}})=0\mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{C}=0\Rightarrow \quad a+1+c=0$
(iii Addition of Eqs. (i), (ii) and (iii),
$\begin{array}{l}
2(a+b+c)+3=0 \\
a+b+c=-\frac{3}{2}
\end{array}
$\Rightarrow \quad-1+c=-$\frac{3}{2}\begin{aligned}$ c &=-$\frac{3}{2}+1 \\ \text{ and } =-\frac{1}{2}=0.5 \\
a \text{ and } =-\frac{1}{2}$\\
b &=-$\frac{1}{2}$\\
c &=-$\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}$

According to the question, Length of the rectangle, $l=1 \mathrm{ m}$ and breadth, $b=50 \mathrm{ cm}=0.5 \mathrm{ m}\therefore$ Area of rectangle, $A=l \times b\begin{aligned}
& \therefore & \ln A & =\ln l+\ln b \\
& \Rightarrow & \frac{\delta A}{A} & =\frac{\delta l}{l}+\frac{\delta b}{b}
\end{aligned}$
Here, $\frac{\delta l}{l}=\frac{\delta b}{b}=1 \%=0.01\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad \delta A & =A\left(\frac{\delta l}{l}+\frac{\delta b}{b}\right) \quad[\because A=l \times b=1 \times 0.5] \\
& =1 \times 0.5(0.01+0.01)=0.01
\end{aligned}$
Area of the table including error is $A^{\prime}=A \pm \delta A\Rightarrow \quad A^{\prime}=(0.5 \pm 0.01) \mathrm{m}^2$
